fact WorkItem(id: "WI-762", description: some(value: "Distributive projection: mark the desugaring at the producer instead of reverse-engineering it in the typer. CONTEXT: WI-639 desugars r.(f1,f2) to a name-keyed tuple (f1: r.f1, ...) sharing ONE receiver TermId, discarding the fact that it WAS a projection; the typer then RECOVERS that fact heuristically. WI-732 had to add a THIRD heuristic to that stack, so it now reads: receiver IDENTITY by source span (projection_receivers_same rung 3 -- Rc::ptr_eq fails because the shared TermId does not survive as a shared Rc, and leaf_sym is None for a computed receiver), receiver TYPE by a stamp the DotApply frame now writes onto the raw receiver occurrence (projection_receiver_type rung 3, which had no producer before), and the LOWERED receiver by reading pos_args[0] of whatever the field typed into, cross-checked by type equality (lowered_projection_receiver -- needed because a computed receiver reaches eval only as the WI-722 macro's where_run rewrite; handing eval the raw node raised 'unhandled Expr variant in eval: DotApply'). Each is individually tested, but all three are inferences about a fact convert.rs KNEW and threw away. The pre-WI-732 consequence of the identity heuristic being incomplete was a SILENT mis-typing: r.where(..).(name,age) typed as (name: Relation[String], age: Relation[Int64]) -- two independent single-column relations, two where evaluations -- and was loud only by accident, when the caller went on to use the result as a relation. PROPOSAL: carry a provenance mark from convert.rs's DistributiveProjection build frame (the WI-618 minted-accessor precedent, mint_op_node) so the typer recognizes a projection because it IS one. ACCEPTANCE: the typer no longer infers projection-hood from span/stamp/position; the three heuristics are retired or reduced to one provenance read; existing wi714_project + wi732 suites green; a hand-written tuple of column accesses on one relation still reads as a projection (proposal 052) OR the change deliberately narrows that and says so."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-714"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "user", at: "2026-07-22T11:39:35Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-762", author: "user", content: "RENUMBERED WI-760 -> WI-762 on merge with origin/main. A different ticket was filed upstream as WI-760 at 16:49Z (codegen gets a resolving KnowledgeBase); this one was filed locally later the same day. Applied the WI-752/WI-753 precedent rule: the number stays with the side filed first and carrying references. Upstream WI-760 is cited by name in the feedback of BOTH WI-089 and WI-576, while this one was referenced only from its own unpushed commit message. NOTE commit 85db6f98 still reads \"WI-760 filed\" for this ticket.", at: "2026-07-18T21:30:14Z")
